 "audit": "Hypermutated tumors (>100 mutations, 21 cases, mostly malignant glioma) were excluded from testing since they inflate every gene. Diagnosis labels are heterogeneous and overlapping (NOS, missing, Unknown, near-duplicate labels such as medulloblastoma subtypes and rhabdomyosarcoma variants), and many diagnoses have very few cases. The cohort is pooled from several studies, so batch and sequencing-platform effects may drive some signals. The comparison group is other tumors in a mixed cohort, not matched tissue. I did not correct for gene length, so large genes may be overcalled. Only about 232 diagnosis-gene pairs with at least 3 mutated cases and 8 cases were tested. I found far fewer novel associations than the ten the PI requested; the few that look new (PIK3R1 in pilocytic astrocytoma, ARID1B in RMS, ZMYM3 in glioma, ASXL1 in medulloblastoma) are single-cohort associations without recurrent hotspots and need independent validation. I did not pad the list with weaker signals to reach ten.",
 "methods": "Counted cases per diagnosis with any non-synonymous mutation per gene, excluded hypermutated cases, ran one-sided Fisher exact tests (diagnosis versus all other tumors) for pairs with at least 3 mutated cases in diagnoses with at least 8 cases, applied Benjamini-Hochberg across tested pairs, kept q < 1e-3 or so, and checked variant patterns for hotspots. Probabilities reflect q-values, effect size and prior literature knowledge."
}